  "habitat": "Flocks on plains with short grass and burned ground. It habitually runs rather than flies.",
  "summary": "A fairly common summer visitor. It is a large, long-legged, thin-billed plover with a white eyebrow. In breeding plumage the breast-band is chestnut; the non-breeding band is dusky. The breeding female may have an incomplete rufous band, and the dark lower edge is always absent. The immature is like the non-breeding adult, though the band may be only a patch on each side. Breeding males are often seen in February and March. The call is a shrill ku-wit.",
